+
+### Evidence Inspection and Native Interaction Owners
+
+`useEvidenceFocus.ts` keeps singular **focused evidence** separate from plural
+viewer selection in `UISettingsAtom.tsx`. Both focus and navigation intent are
+scoped by route, selected source version, document identity and PDF hash. Leaving
+that scope clears them; closing the Extract pane retains them. Focus does not
+change saved findings, quotation associations, labels or review outcomes.
+
+`Selection.tsx` combines local pointer and keyboard ownership with page-wide
+hover from `usePdfEvidenceInteraction.ts`. These temporary label owners do not
+change focused evidence. Label controls and their native editor retain temporary
+ownership during pointer transfer or keyboard use. Eligibility comes from native
+annotation/label filters before inspection: filtered evidence stays absent and
+remembers its focus for restoration. On Hover shows an eligible label for hover,
+keyboard focus or evidence focus; Always shows every eligible label; Hide hides
+all labels while retaining eligible highlights. Explicit URL display modes persist.
+
+`usePdfEvidenceInteraction.ts` finds evidence covering the actual page point,
+deduplicates annotation identities and advances a stable continuous cycle.
+Keyboard Enter/Space uses each reachable highlight's center. A stationary touch
+uses the browser's compatibility click; movement, held touches, cancellation and
+multitouch exclude evidence activation. `SelectionLayer.tsx` retains native drag
+and held-touch text selection, copying and annotation/link creation. Evidence
+movement admission and native long-press cancellation use distinct thresholds.
+
+`utils/pdfEvidenceInteraction.ts` centralizes native interaction owners. Hover
+excludes anchors so PDF links can reveal underlying labels; activation and native
+mouse/touch selection include anchors. Annotation labels, buttons, non-evidence
+role buttons, selection menus and child dialogs own their gestures. The desktop
+and mobile fullscreen knowledge-base shells remain interactive PDF containers.
+`SelectionBoundary.tsx` places label anchors separately above highlight surfaces
+and raises the label in use without changing page geometry or overlap candidates.
+
+Escape follows native owners before the `useEvidenceFocusEscape` window-bubbling
+fallback: child dialogs, rendered filters/settings, annotation actions, pending
+mouse/touch selection, selection menus and browser text ranges handle their first
+Escape. Native child-dialog cancellation restores its launcher. Only an eligible
+PDF Escape with no earlier owner clears focused evidence.
 
